import gunbc.recurring_failure_mode { RecurringFailureMode }

data receipt_consumer_without_producer: RecurringFailureMode = RecurringFailureMode {
  identity: "receipt_consumer_without_producer" as NonEmptyStr,
  receipts: [
    "2026-10-09, PR #13607: srv1 commissioning refused the absent /var/lib/gunbc/microvm-network/converged-slot-network.txt. The earlier observer only wrote a job artifact; no production route published the root-owned receipt the controller consumes. Repair: the installer creates the root-owned receipt directory, and runner_microvm_network_initialize_local_wet binds the local administrator, host and clean source revision, observes all existing convergence predicates, and atomically creates the receipt. A retry observes the same stored generation anew and compares it without replacement; mismatched or unreadable state refuses. Publication admits only this live observer, never caller-supplied receipt text. External network truth remains a live acceptance obligation; no unit test alone establishes it.",
    "2026-10-09 srv1 workspace image run 37878358778, PR #13607: the compiler pair built successfully, then release-bins packing refused BuildDiagnosticsMissing because the product requires gunbc-floor-cmd.log but fleet's pair build dispatch ran the raw cargo line without the floor's capture wrapper. The pack's refusal was correct. Reusing wrap_command_with_floor_attempt_receipt at that producer captures the required diagnostics and preserves compiler failure through tee; no empty log is synthesized and no pack member is dropped.",
    "2026-10-09 srv1 workspace bringup, PR #13607: allocation offer admission and the controller require a gateway forwarding observation no older than 60 seconds, but workspace_refresh_gateway_wet had no production caller. The observer existed and its decoder was tested, while every real offer necessarily refused an absent or stale receipt. A bounded foreground operator refresher was initially added, then removed when the operator selected direct SSH from srv1. That route does not exercise gateway forwarding and must not require its receipt: workspace_ssh_access now carries distinct host-local and gateway routes, and each consumer requires only the evidence for its enrolled route. Gateway clients retain their forwarding-proof requirement. Host-local acceptance still requires the invocation-bound guest host key and authenticated guest SSH; a fresh host observation alone is not a login receipt.",
    "PR #12421 review 5331195485: gunbc_ci_namecheap_observe_invoke supplied receipt_rel as though it captured execution output, but gunbc_invoke_receipt_steps only read an existing file. A successful observer therefore failed the shell step and suppressed its artifact upload. Invalid state: an emitted receipt read with no producer. Harm: successful observation becomes workflow failure. Discriminating facts: execute emitted shell in a clean root with only the declared output; a planted unmatched read must fail. Mitigation: writer, console display and uploader derive the path from one declaration. Ceiling: workflow construction rejects a receipt consumer without a producer edge; next trigger: that consumed workflow admission relation.",
  ],
  evidence: [],
}
